This file credits third-party code and data that ameriflux-mcp ports, derives from or
vendors (DESIGN.md D27). Each entry is added, with the full upstream licence text, by
the build step that brings the material into the repository.

Current contents
----------------

None. As of build step 1 the repository contains no third-party code or data. The
research notes (RESEARCH.md, research/) quote short passages from public AmeriFlux and
FLUXNET web pages, data-policy text and API responses for reference, with their sources.

Planned entries
---------------

- amerifluxr (https://github.com/chuhousen/amerifluxr), BSD-3-Clause: the variable-name
  parsing logic of amf_parse_basename (step 5) and the US-CRT sample files used as test
  fixtures (step 6).
- FLUXNET Shuttle (https://github.com/fluxnet/shuttle), BSD-3-Clause: the FLUXNET v1.3+
  zip filename pattern (step 6).
- ONEFlux (https://github.com/fluxnet/ONEFlux), LBNL BSD-3-Clause with the
  Enhancements clause: units derived from var_info_definitions_{hh,dd,ww,mm,yy}.txt
  (step 5).
- FLUXNET2015 variable dictionaries
  (https://ftp.fluxdata.org/.fluxnet_downloads_67934/webdoc/variable_codes_{FULLSET,SUBSET}_20200504.csv):
  no licence is stated, so only derived tables are committed, with source URL, fetch date
  and ETag (step 5; licence question Q7 in research/questions.md).
- US-CRT sample data are AmeriFlux data under CC-BY-4.0, not BSD: Jiquan Chen, Housen Chu,
  AmeriFlux BASE US-CRT Curtice Walter-Berger cropland, Ver. 2-5 (outdated; current is
  Ver. 5-5), AmeriFlux AMP, (Dataset). https://doi.org/10.17190/AMF/1246156. Funding for
  the AmeriFlux data service was provided by the U.S. Department of Energy Office of
  Science.
